  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 22-layer alternating ZnS/MgF2 multilayer filter on CaF2 substrate under normal incidence. Layer sequence: ZnS(1), MgF2(2), ZnS(3), MgF2(4), ZnS(5), MgF2(6), ZnS(7), MgF2(8), ZnS(9), MgF2(10), ZnS(11), MgF2(12), ZnS(13), MgF2(14), ZnS(15), MgF2(16), ZnS(17), MgF2(18), ZnS(19), MgF2(20), ZnS(21), MgF2(22). Initialize all 22 thicknesses from empirical mean of iteration 01 top candidates (approximately 950nm mean) with Gaussian perturbation standard deviation 150nm. Constrain thickness bounds to [400, 1600]nm per layer. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with step size reduced by 40% relative to standard. Evaluate transmittance at four wavelength bands: passbands 3250-3350nm and 4200-4300nm (maximize), stopbands 2500-3100nm and 4450-5000nm (minimize). Score via equal-weight mean aggregation across bands. Air incidence, CaF2 substrate, no metal layers, coherent TMM solver. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 2500-3100 nm, 3250-3350 nm, 4200-4300 nm, 4450-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 3.25-3.35 um and 4.20-4.30 um bands; Low transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count <= 24; No metal layers; Conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials only.",
